<resources>
	<!-- Example customization of dimensions originally defined in res/values/dimens.xml
         (such as screen margins) for screens with more than 820dp of available width. This
         would include 7" and 10" devices in landscape (~960dp and ~1280dp respectively). -->
	<dimen name="activity_horizontal_margin">64dp</dimen>

	<!-- Wide-screen flight mini-map. The Autel Smart Controller V3 measures 1024 x 720 dp
	     (verified over adb), where the 160dp square from values-h440dp is
	     lost in the empty space either side of the video.

	     Deliberately NOT square. Width drives the whole HUD column (EV slider, EV scale,
	     exposure readout) and every dp of it is taken from the video, so it only goes to
	     180dp. Height costs nothing but vertical room, of which there is a lot, so the map
	     gets 240dp.

	     Height budget re-checked, since the base entry warns that overflow here is SILENT —
	     the map is the column's last child and simply gets clipped off the bottom. Above the
	     map is ~233dp, so 240dp needs ~473dp of screen height against the V3's measured
	     720dp. Comfortable. A hypothetical device wider than 820dp but under ~500dp tall
	     would clip; no controller in this project's scope is that shape.

	     Smaller hardware (e.g. a Smart Controller SE) does not reach 820dp of width and keeps
	     the square 160dp from values-h440dp — that bucket must stay usable. -->
	<dimen name="flight_map_size">180dp</dimen>
	<dimen name="flight_map_height">240dp</dimen>

	<!-- flight_map_size (180dp here) + flightHudColumn's paddingEnd (14dp) — see the base
	     entry's comment. It was once hardcoded at the base bucket's
	     144dp everywhere, ~50dp short of this bucket's real map edge. -->
	<dimen name="flight_resource_row_margin_end">194dp</dimen>

	<!-- Readout column text (Clock / SPI overlay / gimbal pitch / FAA ceiling / RTH altitude).
	     12sp is hard to read on the V3's real screen size at
	     normal viewing distance, even though it reads fine on smaller hardware at the same
	     dp value (a smaller physical screen puts the same dp closer to the eye). Bumped to
	     18sp — a clear, deliberate increase, not a rounding nudge. Smaller hardware (Smart
	     Controller SE, and similar) keeps the base 12sp from values/dimens.xml; this bucket is the V3
	     specifically, same reasoning as flight_map_size above. -->
	<dimen name="flight_readout_text_size">18sp</dimen>

	<!-- CrosshairView stroke widths, ~25% heavier than the base bucket's exact-current-appearance
	     values (see values/dimens.xml's comment): the reticle
	     reads too fine on the V3's real screen. 3px->3.75px, 1.5px->1.875px, 6px->7.5px. -->
	<dimen name="crosshair_arm_outline_width">3.75px</dimen>
	<dimen name="crosshair_arm_line_width">1.875px</dimen>
	<dimen name="crosshair_ring_width">3.75px</dimen>
	<dimen name="crosshair_ring_outline_width">7.5px</dimen>

	<!-- Heavier than the base bucket: these readouts are 18sp (36px) here, and an outline
	     sized for 12sp disappears against a bright scene. 2dp is 4px, about an eighth of the
	     text size — the stroke is centred, so half of that is covered by the fill. See
	     OutlinedTextView; going much above this fills the letters in. -->
	<dimen name="hud_text_outline_width">2dp</dimen>

    <!-- ⚠ BOTH TOOLBAR CAPSULES MUST BE THIS TALL, AND IT IS A MINIMUM, NOT A HEIGHT.
         The two clusters hold different things, so they measure differently: the ACTIONS
         capsule's tallest child is the 46dp drop pin and the STATUS capsule's is a 34dp icon.
         Two capsules that begin on the same line and end on different ones read as a mistake.

         ⚠ IT IS DERIVED, NOT CHOSEN: the actions capsule's natural height, which is the drop
         pin plus the capsule's own paddingVertical on each side.

             46dp drop pin + 2 x 3dp paddingVertical = 52dp

         A value BELOW that does nothing at all === the actions capsule is already taller, and
         the status capsule stays short; at 40dp the capsules were not level.
         If the drop pin or the padding changes, this changes with them.

         A MINIMUM rather than a fixed height because either cluster may still grow: a longer
         signal readout, a taller button style, a density not yet seen. minHeight can only make
         a capsule taller, thus it can never clip its own content. -->
    <dimen name="hud_capsule_height">52dp</dimen>

</resources>
